{
  "version": 3,
  "name": "UREI 1176LN Rev D",
  "category": "Dynamics",
  "author": "LiveWDF",
  "description": "UREI 1176LN Rev D, factory drawing for serials 1239\u20132331. The selected 2N5457, discrete preamp, dual-phase feedback rectifier, attack and release network, and transformer-loaded class-A line amplifier use the service topology. The modeled balanced connections are ground-referenced. SPICE transistor transport parameters, nominal linear transformer winding equivalents, stabilized bias, and an input pot substitute for selected parts, coupled iron, a user-adjustable factory trim, and the T attenuator. R86 is fixed at 30 ohms in the factory R85/R86 series feedback path. A Q5 emitter load stabilizes the discrete solve. The discrete detector senses the pre-makeup signal. Ratio continuously changes detector drive. The VU meter, linked unit, mains supply and mechanically ganged pushbutton assembly are outside the audio model.",
  "io": {
    "groundNode": "0",
    "inputNode": "in",
    "outputNode": "out"
  },
